t through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect Continuous vs. Present Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use these tenses  to express that an action began in the past and is still going on or has just finished. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We use the <span class=\"italic\">Present Perfect tense</span> mainly to express that an action is completed or to emphasize the result. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Forms:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Regular verbs: form of <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + base form of verb + <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Example: I have worked at the bakery for six years.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<br/>Irregular verbs: form of <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + past participle of irregular verbs", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Example: I have written a number of books in the last two years.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<br/>We use the <span class=\"italic\">Present Perfect Continuous tense</span> to emphasize the duration or continuous course of an action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Form:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Form of <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + <span class=\"italic\">been</span> + base form of verb + <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Example: We have been walking for two hours!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Because you are talking about the continuous course of an action, you often use a time marker with Present Perfect Continuous tense, like:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>for two hours</li><li>for a long time</li><li>for ages</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I've been in touch with the editors of \"Cambridge Life\". ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've decided it would be boring to be a scientist. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've been wanting to be a journalist for ages!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've been planning to enrol in some courses for a while.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Discussing How to Deal with Problems ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to offer advice or give solutions to a problem, you use modals like <span class=\"italic\">might, should</span> or <span class=\"italic\">could</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "These modals can go at the beginning of the sentence, or after a clause starting with <span class=\"italic\">\u201cIf ... \u201d</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The modal is followed by a verb in the base form. You do not use \u201cto\u201d. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I would/I'd ... <br/>I wouldn't ... <br/>You could ... <br/>You should ...", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I would keep my options open.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You could talk to a few more people first.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Maybe you should think a bit more about this idea. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "it looks promising", "type": "name"}, {"content": "expression meaning \u201cI feel positive or optimistic\u201d about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Well, it's not 100% sure yet, but it looks promising! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about personality related to jobs.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "self-motivated", "type": "name"}, {"content": "describes a person who does not need other people to encourage them to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They think I'm self-motivated, ambitious, a real go-getter!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "scientist", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who studies science as a profession", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You have also talked a lot about being a scientist.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rational", "type": "name"}, {"content": "based on human reason", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Scientists have to be rational all the time.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "logical", "type": "name"}, {"content": "based on logic or reason; not abstract", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A scientist is usually quite logical.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to jump to a decision", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to decide something quickly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I wouldn't jump to any decisions.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "introvert", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who does not like to talk to people very much", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're a bit of an introvert. I see you more as a scientist.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, make a list of 20 adjectives that describe personality, like <span class=\"italic\">shy</span>, <span class=\"italic\">reserved</span>, <span class=\"italic\">outgoing</span>, etc.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk to 5 different people. Ask each person to identify 4 adjectives on the list that best describe their personality.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask each person if they are an extrovert or an introvert.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, discuss different careers or do research online. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find one career that goes with the personality of each person. You can choose funny or unusual careers.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Inform the 5 people about what career you selected for them. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain your choice and give suggestions about what the person should do.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about personality.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask questions about personality.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss and read about personality types that go with different careers.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain the career choice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give suggestions.", "type": "text"}]}]}